        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s recap some of the rules for exponents.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's recap some of the rules for exponents.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<ul><li><p><strong>Product rule</strong>: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.</p></li><li><p><strong>Quotient rule</strong>: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.</p></li><li><p><strong>Power rule</strong>: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.</p></li><li><p><strong>Power of product rule</strong>: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.</p></li><li><p><strong>Power of quotient rule</strong>: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.</p></li></ul>",
            "readable_text": "- Product rule: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.\n- Quotient rule: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.\n- Power rule: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.\n- Power of product rule: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.\n- Power of quotient rule: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let&#x27;s see an example of this.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nLet's recap some of the rules for exponents.\n\nContent:\n- Product rule: to multiply powers of the same base, add the exponents.\n- Quotient rule: to divide powers of the same base, subtract the exponents.\n- Power rule: to raise a power to another power, multiply the exponents.\n- Power of product rule: to raise the product of two numbers to a power, raise each number to that power, and then multiply.\n- Power of quotient rule: to raise a fraction to a power, raise both the numerator and the denominator to that power.\n\nContent:\nWe can use a combination of these rules to simplify expressions containing exponents. Let's see an example of this."
      },
