        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}]</span> as a base raised to a single number.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}] as a base raised to a single number.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we rewrite the numerator using the product rule for exponents:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}= \\dfrac{5^{4+2}}{5^3} = \\dfrac{5^{6}}{5^3}]</span></p><p>Then, we use the quotient rule for exponents:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{5^6}{5^3} = 5^{6-3} = 5^{3}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we rewrite the numerator using the product rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}= \\dfrac{5^{4+2}}{5^3} = \\dfrac{5^{6}}{5^3}]\n\nThen, we use the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{5^6}{5^3} = 5^{6-3} = 5^{3}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}] as a base raised to a single number.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we rewrite the numerator using the product rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{5^4\\cdot 5^2}{5^3}= \\dfrac{5^{4+2}}{5^3} = \\dfrac{5^{6}}{5^3}]\n\nThen, we use the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{5^6}{5^3} = 5^{6-3} = 5^{3}]"
      },
