        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{7}{4}\\right)^5]</span> as the product of two exponentiated integers.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{7}{4}\\right)^5] as the product of two exponentiated integers.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of quotient rule:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4^{8} \u22c5 ((7)/(4))^{5} = 4^{8} \u22c5 (7^{5})/(4^{5})]</span></p><p>Next, we rewrite the fractional part of our expression as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot  \\dfrac{7^5}{4^5} =  \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5]</span></p><p>Finally, we simplify using the quotient rule for exponents:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5 =4^{8-5}\\cdot 7^5=4^{3}\\cdot 7^5]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we rewrite the second factor using the power of quotient rule:\n\n[MATH: 4^{8} \u22c5 ((7)/(4))^{5} = 4^{8} \u22c5 (7^{5})/(4^{5})]\n\nNext, we rewrite the fractional part of our expression as follows:\n\n[MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{7^5}{4^5} = \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5]\n\nFinally, we simplify using the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5 =4^{8-5}\\cdot 7^5=4^{3}\\cdot 7^5]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{7}{4}\\right)^5] as the product of two exponentiated integers.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we rewrite the second factor using the power of quotient rule:\n\n[MATH: 4^{8} \u22c5 ((7)/(4))^{5} = 4^{8} \u22c5 (7^{5})/(4^{5})]\n\nNext, we rewrite the fractional part of our expression as follows:\n\n[MATH: 4^{8} \\cdot \\dfrac{7^5}{4^5} = \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5]\n\nFinally, we simplify using the quotient rule for exponents:\n\n[MATH: \\dfrac{4^8}{4^5} \\cdot 7^5 =4^{8-5}\\cdot 7^5=4^{3}\\cdot 7^5]"
      },
